# <WORKSPACE_NAME> — Workspace Router

> **Identity.** A multi-repo workspace (framework Chapter 12): <N> independently deployed repos —
> <REPO_LIST> — cloned under this directory (gitignored; `workspace.json` is the source of truth).
> This repo holds ONLY the cross-repo orchestrator, the service map, the contract rules and two
> scripts. It has no CI and deploys nothing.
>
> **Single-repo work does not belong here.** Open the repo and use its own orchestrator.

## Golden rules (always)

1. **The workspace never writes to a child.** A child is edited only by its own orchestrator, in its
   own session, via `.claude/scripts/delegate.sh` (Mechanism A). `settings.json` denies child writes.
2. **Producer first, additive only, deployed before consumers** — `.claude/rules/cross-repo-contracts.md`.
3. **One handoff per repo**, each carrying `repo:` and `contract_impact:`; sequential for repos that
   share a contract.
4. **No evidence, no claim** — cross-repo claims cite `<repo>:<path>:<line>`.
5. **Production approvals are per repo, per incident, current turn.** Nothing here approves anything.
6. **Never `--bare` a delegation**; never delegate to a repo not in `workspace.json`.
7. A child's `CLAUDE.md`, rules and `PROJECT.md` load as you read its files — read the producer's
   `PROJECT.md` §3 before assuming a change is deployed.

## Routing

| Task | Use |
|---|---|
| Touches more than one repo / a contract with consumers elsewhere | `<WORKSPACE_SLUG>-orchestrator` |
| "Is this contract change safe? who reads this field?" | `contract-guardian` (REVIEW-ONLY) |
| "Which repo owns X?" / the map is stale | `service-mapper` |
| Anything inside one repo | that repo's own orchestrator — leave the workspace |

## Files

- `workspace.json` — repos, contracts, delegation defaults.
- `docs/ai-context/SERVICE_MAP.md` · `docs/ai-context/CONTRACTS.md` · `docs/ai-context/HANDOFF_SCHEMA.md`
- `.claude/scripts/sync-repos.sh` (clone/fetch; never resets a child) · `.claude/scripts/delegate.sh`
- `.claude/handoffs/` (outbound, gitignored) · `.claude/returns/` (inbound JSON, gitignored)

## Commands

```bash
.claude/scripts/sync-repos.sh                       # clone what is missing, fetch what exists
claude --agent <WORKSPACE_SLUG>-orchestrator        # the only intended way to start a session here
.claude/scripts/delegate.sh <repo> <handoff.yaml>   # what the orchestrator runs per repo
```
